 "provenance": {
  "bevel": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "photo-measured - the small housing has the large one's octagonal section at its own size. The front's silhouette narrows about 9 mm at its top and bottom rows and reaches full width about 15-16 mm in, at every corner, so the four depth-wise edges are bevelled [9, 16] (the image's mask quantises to 1.8 mm). The legend plate is 44.5 of the 72.1 mm face, so the edges where the front and back meet the finned sides are bevelled 13.8, taken at 45 degrees as on the large housing, whose video shows the same bands."
  },
  "bottom-layout": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - not photographed; drawn bare (see the underside gap)."
  },
  "chassis": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet - 'Dimension (L*W*H) 4.33 x 3.66 x 2.84 in'. As on the large housing the letters are not width, height and depth: the straight-on front reads within 2.5 percent of 2.84/4.33 = 0.656 wide-to-tall, so L (110.0 mm) is the face's height as the unit hangs on the rail, H (72.1) its width and W (93.0) the depth."
  },
  "front-layout": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "photo-measured on the straight-on AIS2002 front image at 4.427 px/mm from the datasheet's 110 mm face height (Gate 1: the face's own width agrees to 1-2.5 percent). Lamps located by colour: the control row at y 8.6 (PWR 27.5, SYS 32.6, the SFP lamps 9 and 10 at 37.7 and 42.75); jack lamps in columns at x 26.6 and 48.3, rows on a 15.77 mm pitch from y 24.4; the SFP pair x 25.0-50.0, y 87.6-102.1, between two gold number strips. Jacks are drawn with the lamped ganged cell turned 90/270 so the keyways face out (its lamps 8.3 mm apart against the jacks' 11), cages std/sfp@1 on their side, left 270 and right 90. The reset hole is not visible against the dark plate in the image; it is drawn under its legend, where the large housing has it."
  },
  "lamps": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "photo-measured - each jack has ONE lamp, green, at its top (the PoE builds add an amber one below it), and the colour key names only LINK/ACT; drawn with common/rj45-ganged-link@1, the right-hand column with its lamp-right skin."
  },
  "power": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet - 'Power Supply DC 12-55 V'; 'Idling: 12V 1.99W / 55V 2.48W'; 'Full load: 12V 6.71W / 55V 6.99W'. power-max-w takes the highest figure (6.99 W); no ambient is stated with any of them. The supply is not included ('the power supply is excluded from the package')."
  },
  "rear-layout": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - the back render is foreshortened top to bottom; widths are taken as fractions of the face on the same image row, heights as fractions of 110 mm and fitted to the face. An upper wall plate with its screws above the keyholes, the DIN clip, and a lower plate with its screws below, centred; the 42 mm plate (common/wall-plate-keyhole-2-42@1) because the large housing's 56 mm one would overrun the 44.5 mm flat. The DIN rail's centre line lies about 55 mm from the top of this face."
  },
  "side-layout": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - from the three-quarter image: the sides are fins running front to back between the bevels, with a recessed channel and a raised badge plate carrying the wordmark on the right side. The left side is not photographed and is drawn as fins only."
  },
  "silkscreen": {
   "confidence": "photo-measured",
   "note": "photo-measured - legends transcribed from the AIS2002 front image: Reset, PWR, SYS, 9, 10; Fast Ring and SCP with leaders to switches 1 and 2; LINK/ACT under its colour key; the port numbers, odd on the left; the SFP numbers on their gold strips; the summary line '8 x GE | 2 x GE SFP' up the left. The AURCORE wordmark is printed as text: its A is drawn as a chevron mark, which is not reproduced (no logo marks)."
  },
  "sources": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "vendor datasheet (AIS2002 Data Sheet 1.0, 3 pages: spec table, and an annotated front and back figure that is the same artwork as the product images); the product page's three images (straight-on front, three-quarter front-top-right, and a back render raised to show the top face), 1000 px. No hardware guide or drawing is published, and the vendor video shows only the large housing."
  },
  "surge": {
   "confidence": "datasheet",
   "note": "datasheet - the AIS2002 data sheet states two figures: its feature list says 'Common mode 4KV' and its specification table 'Common mode 6KV'. The table is taken, as it agrees with the AIS2001, AIS2001P and AIS2002P; the 4 kV bullet may be carried over from another model and is unresolved."
  },
  "top-layout": {
   "confidence": "estimated",
   "note": "estimated - no straight-on top view exists. Positions are fractions of the top face in the back render (image 3), corrected with the parts' own sizes: the five-way power header runs front to back (its 35.56 mm reading 35 on the render) with its pole legend '1 + - earth + - 2' on one side and POWER:12-55V DC on the other, pole 1 at the rear; the RELAY header behind it; the CONSOLE jack behind that, a bare RJ45 with its keyway toward the front - the console is on the top face of the small housing, where the large one has it on the front; the ground screw and its earth symbol at the front edge. Good to a few millimetres."
  }
 },
